00:34:15.918 --> 00:34:16.228
Yeah,

00:34:16.388 --> 00:34:17.138
so it's high.

00:34:17.148 --> 00:34:17.498
Why?

00:34:17.748 --> 00:34:20.779
Because 72 is H and 73 is I.

00:34:20.989 --> 00:34:23.938
Now some of you said hi fairly emphatically why.

00:34:24.268 --> 00:34:24.349
Well,

00:34:24.398 --> 00:34:26.947
33 turns out you wouldn't know this unless you looked

00:34:26.947 --> 00:34:29.947
it up or someone told you is an exclamation point.

00:34:30.069 --> 00:34:32.309
So literally if you were to text someone like right now,

00:34:32.388 --> 00:34:33.299
if you haven't already,

00:34:33.467 --> 00:34:35.908
HI exclamation point in all caps.

00:34:36.013 --> 00:34:40.434
You would essentially be sending 3 bytes of information somehow over the internet

00:34:40.773 --> 00:34:45.373
to that recipient and because their phone similarly understands ASCI

00:34:45.373 --> 00:34:47.914
because it was programmed years ago to do so,

00:34:48.164 --> 00:34:52.444
it knows to show you HI exclamation point and not a number,

00:34:52.643 --> 00:34:53.592
3 numbers no less,

00:34:53.684 --> 00:34:55.924
or colors or something else altogether.

00:34:56.270 --> 00:34:58.070
So here we then have high,

00:34:58.459 --> 00:34:59.889
3 digits in a row here.

00:35:00.379 --> 00:35:01.820
