00:35:37.219 --> 00:35:37.719
32,

00:35:37.729 --> 00:35:39.209
and that pattern continues.

00:35:39.409 --> 00:35:40.090
What does this mean?

00:35:40.175 --> 00:35:40.405
Well,

00:35:40.645 --> 00:35:41.485
computers know how to do this.

00:35:41.645 --> 00:35:43.475
Most normal humans don't need this information,

00:35:43.604 --> 00:35:46.314
but what it means is if you are representing

00:35:46.514 --> 00:35:47.514
in binary

00:35:47.685 --> 00:35:49.965
with your transistors on and off representing some pattern,

00:35:50.004 --> 00:35:51.024
and this is the pattern

00:35:51.445 --> 00:35:52.745
representing capital letter A,

00:35:52.965 --> 00:35:55.594
which is why we have a 1 in the 604 space and a 1

00:35:55.844 --> 00:35:56.955
in the ones place,

00:35:57.364 --> 00:36:01.514
how does a computer go about lower casing this same letter?

00:36:02.125 --> 00:36:02.475
Yeah.

00:36:05.489 --> 00:36:05.889
Perfect.

00:36:05.969 --> 00:36:11.320
All the computer has to do is change this one bit in the 32's place to a 1,

00:36:11.530 --> 00:36:14.610
because that has the effect mathematically per our discussion of adding

00:36:14.919 --> 00:36:16.840
the number 32 to whatever it is.

00:36:16.929 --> 00:36:19.489
So it turns out you can force text from upper case

00:36:19.489 --> 00:36:22.850
to lower case or back by just changing a single bit.

00:36:23.419 --> 00:36:24.739
Inside of that pattern

00:36:25.020 --> 00:36:26.790
of 8 bits in total.

